lifeos-nix patch f-inference-provider — local model server, Anthropic as fallback, local-only airtight

PROBLEM
  LifeOS can only talk to Anthropic. `claude` is the sole model client, and Inference.ts
  actively deletes ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL. There is no way to run on a local LLM server, and no
  way to keep Anthropic as a safety net — or to forbid it — when one is used.

FIX
  One switch in the USER-zone config, LIFEOS/USER/CONFIG/LIFEOS_CONFIG.toml:

    [inference]
    mode = "local-only"              # anthropic-only | local-with-fallback | local-only
                                     # (default when [inference.local] is set: local-with-fallback)
    [inference.local]
    base_url  = "http://host:port"   # must speak Anthropic /v1/messages
    model     = "name"               # all tiers; [inference.local.models] overrides per tier
    token_env = "VAR"                # optional

  - NEW LIFEOS/TOOLS/InferenceProvider.ts — the one decision. `gate` subcommand is run by the
    lifeos-nix claude wrapper (pkgs/tools/misc/claude-code/claude-gate.sh) before EVERY exec of
    the real binary, so the launcher, Inference.ts, Pulse, skills and a bare `claude` all pass
    through it; it prints the env delta as shell code and the wrapper execs in place.
  - LifeosConfig.ts: loadRawLifeosConfig() — the TOML without identity validation, uncached.
  - Inference.ts: picks the target per call; local-with-fallback retries once on Anthropic
    when the local attempt fails, with every local variable stripped (anthropicEnv); local-only
    fails closed. Spawns carry LIFEOS_INFERENCE_TARGET so the gate honours the choice. The local
    target maps tiers/pinned ids to local model names and verifies the executed model by name.

  local-only is fail-closed at every layer (code review 2026-10-04 found the v1 two-seam
  design leaking through Pulse, 11 scrub-and-spawn tools, WebFetch's domain preflight, typo'd
  keys and unreadable configs):
  - a present section with an unknown key or bad value refuses (a typo never picks a mode);
  - LIFEOS_INFERENCE_MODE=local-only is exported into the session; every descendant is
    local-only regardless of what it can read, and refuses if it cannot read the local table;
  - a child that scrubs BASE_URL/AUTH_TOKEN gets the local env back from the gate at exec;
  - an explicit Anthropic request (target hint) under local-only refuses;
  - CLAUDE_CODE_DISABLE_NONESSENTIAL_TRAFFIC, CLAUDE_CODE_DISABLE_WEB_FETCH (WebFetch asks
    api.anthropic.com about every domain first) and ENABLE_CLAUDEAI_MCP_SERVERS=false;
  - the gate refuses on any error, including its own crash; LIFEOS_GATE=off is the only bypass.
  Not covered here: the Agent SDK runs its own bundled binary, not the wrapper — its users
  (Siri, iMessage) are retired/disabled (f-siri-retire); a network-level block is ISA Step 7c.

VERIFIED GOTCHA (why AUTH_TOKEN is always set on the local target)
  With only ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL set, Claude Code sends the subscription OAuth bearer token to
  that URL (measured 2026-10-04: BASE_URL alone → the token arrived; with a placeholder
  AUTH_TOKEN → no `sk-ant-` value in any header). AUTH_TOKEN outranks OAuth, so a server
  without auth gets "lifeos-local-no-auth", never the subscription credential.

SCOPE / CO-EXISTENCE
  One new file + two edited (Inference.ts, LifeosConfig.ts). The launcher (lifeos.ts) is no
  longer touched: the gate in the claude wrapper covers it.

VERIFICATION
  tests/inference-provider/run.sh — resolution and refusals, sticky local-only, env overlay and
  strip, the full decide() table, the real gate script end to end against a recording fake
  claude and an up/down fake server, Inference.ts through the gate. Mutation-checked.

